{"seconds": 0.14963033283129334, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/C06/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "51442ed0e1c6c5b1fe5a9dc8ec69b1b76eabea38057bc4e7b16f2647a49d5887", "code_sha256": "04a4eea4efdb00f50ff5325096b0595d1e4429bf5ca270d878f350e018e44c3f", "description": "High-effort, single-shot solution (one deterministic submission) for CASCADE DS04 held-out animals. The model learns only from training recordings, uses grouped cross-validation on provided animal IDs (not as predictors), and never touches test labels or groups. It builds a compact feature set from each recording\u2019s fluorescence: robustly standardized fluorescence, its first derivative split into positive/negative parts, and a bank of past lags sampled by seconds using each row\u2019s dt. Training frames are weighted so each recording contributes equally and animals are balanced. A ridge regressor (fit_intercept=True) is selected by maximizing grouped-CV Pearson correlation. The final model is refit on all training frames and applied to test rows. Outputs are nonnegative, finite, per-frame expected spike counts at the required 200 ms target resolution; masking is respected and padded frames yield zero. No external files, pretrained weights, or cross-row leakage are used. Deterministic seeds are set. The full implementation is under 240 lines and CPU-light.", "code_lines": 223, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

